<item><title>Uganda wildlife board to review tourism revenue-sharing</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-wildlife-board-to-review-tourism-revenue-sharing-a1d2aa/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-wildlife-board-to-review-tourism-revenue-sharing-a1d2aa/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>Chairman James Kalema says the board will assess whether communities near protected areas benefit effectively from tourism income.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:00:05 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Visa opens Kampala office as Uganda&apos;s central bank demands cheaper payments</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/visa-opens-kampala-office-as-uganda-s-central-bank-demands-c546a6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/visa-opens-kampala-office-as-uganda-s-central-bank-demands-c546a6/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>Governor Michael Atingi-Ego also urged the company to help lenders assess small firms and strengthen protection against rising cybercrime.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:42:27 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Uganda&apos;s Dei BioPharma says it is ready to supply Africa&apos;s medicine market</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-s-dei-biopharma-says-it-is-ready-to-supply-africa-s-931f7d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-s-dei-biopharma-says-it-is-ready-to-supply-africa-s-931f7d/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>Founder Matthias Magoola says the company has more than 500 products and will launch six antimalarial medicines within two weeks.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:33:20 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
